Baseline for scripts/verify-target.sh. The script compares the frozen files
(docs/design/target/, internal/archtest/target_test.go, scripts/verify-target.sh)
with the last commit that touched this file, and lists output changes since then.

Round 2 (2026-10-09): the maintainer lifted byte-identical output. CLI behavior may
change to make the code clean, as long as every change is listed in
docs/design/output-changes.md. Legacy support is dropped: the invoice-tool
directory, the deprecated command forms of #106, and Markdown archived invoices
(with a stderr warning naming the skipped files).

Round 2, ports v2 (2026-10-09): docs/design/ports-v2.md is normative for the ports. The target
test no longer requires a billing.Compiler; render/latex owns the Compiler interface and
adapters/tectonic implements it.

